# RecruitKit — Project Brain

## Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript (`src/app/`)
- PostgreSQL on Supabase via **Prisma** (`@/lib/db`) — not the Supabase JS client
- Clerk auth: `auth()` / `clerkClient()` in server code; Clerk UI components on auth pages
- OpenAI SDK (`gpt-4o`) for generation — plain text responses, not JSON mode
- Tailwind CSS; deploy target is Vercel

## Database (CRITICAL)
- `DATABASE_URL`: Supavisor **transaction** pooler, port **6543**, with `?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1`
- `DIRECT_URL`: Supavisor **session** pooler, port **5432** on `pooler.supabase.com`
- **Never** use `db.*.supabase.co` on IPv4-only networks
- **Never** run `prisma db push` on the shared Supabase project — it will try to drop unrelated tables. Use targeted SQL or `prisma migrate` instead.
- Supabase project ref: `onuzmeyzwrusrzjhqsys`

## Data model
- `User.clerkId` stores the Clerk user ID; `User.id` is the internal cuid primary key
- `Job.userId` references `User.id` (not `clerkId`)
- Free tier: `jdQuota` defaults to 3; check quota before generation

## Auth pattern
- Server actions / server components: `const { userId } = await auth()` — return an error if null
- Resolve app user: `db.user.findUnique({ where: { clerkId: userId } })`
- On first visit: `ensureUser(clerkId, email)` in `@/lib/db` creates the User row
- Middleware in `src/middleware.ts` protects non-public routes via `clerkMiddleware`

## Server actions (preferred over API routes)
- Mutations live in `src/app/actions/` with `"use server"` at the top
- Colocate types as `*.types.ts` next to the action (e.g. `generateJob.types.ts`)
- Return structured state objects `{ error?: string; content?: string; ... }` for `useFormState`
- Call `revalidatePath("/")` after writes
- Wrap DB + OpenAI calls in try/catch

## File structure
- Pages: `src/app/**/page.tsx`
- Server actions: `src/app/actions/`
- Components: `src/components/`
- Lib/helpers: `src/lib/` (`db.ts`, `openai.ts`, `utils.ts`)
- Schema: `prisma/schema.prisma`

## UI conventions
- Match the existing JD generator style (Tailwind, blue primary, clean forms)
- Loading states on async form submissions (`useFormStatus`)
- Empty states on library/list views
- Copy-to-clipboard: `useState` + 2s reset timeout

## Product context
- Micro-SaaS for recruiters/staffing agencies ($49/mo planned)
- **Built:** JD generator + job library
- **Next:** Outreach generator, interview question generator
- **Later:** Stripe billing and usage counters on every generation feature
